cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the deposited artifacts, please cite the article."
title: "tgnn-solv: a thermodynamically structured graph network for solid-liquid solubility"
abstract: >-
  Code and analysis for "Ground Truth That Does Not Ground: Substituting Reference Solvent
  sigma-Profiles Degrades COSMO-SAC Solubility Prediction". Contains the model, the fixed
  COSMO-SAC closure, the decomposition that separates a deployed thermodynamic model's own
  error from what its inputs leave unresolved, and every gate that binds a printed number to
  the artifact it came from.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/doctawho42/tgnn-solv"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Polomoshnov
    given-names: "Nikita L."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4342-8539"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Bioengineering and Bioinformatics, Lomonosov Moscow State University"
  - family-names: Rudik
    given-names: "A. V."
    affiliation: "V. N. Orekhovich Institute of Biomedical Chemistry"
keywords:
  - solubility prediction
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - COSMO-SAC
  - infinite-dilution activity coefficients
  - model misspecification
